KG42.register("clusters-5b1f7e39ce3f61ef53376244",{"id":"05-double_auction::v142-d-CL004","paper":"05-double_auction","label":"Pairwise pricing, trading conditions, and bilateral payments and receipts","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL004","label":"Pairwise pricing, trading conditions, and bilateral payments and receipts","market_meaning":"For winning buyer-seller pairs in M01, the pairwise price is used for trade execution and for the identical payment and receipt rates of the two sides; the transaction-price bounds are linked to the source text's requirement of nonnegative consumer utility. This candidate has not yet achieved closure of the utility definition and monetary settlement.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","pricing","activation","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The correspondence between prices and input quantities is limited to the same winning trading pair, the same auction, and the same predetermined k. The photovoltaic time window in R006 is only case-study context and cannot restrict the general period of applicability of pricing; the participation utility in R007 also does not automatically equal the payoff from strategic bidding.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Trade eligibility, pairwise prices, and the rates for both sides have direct dependencies involving information and obligations, making them suitable for assembly across execution, pricing, participation, and settlement; bidding-strategy selection and welfare optimality are not treated as implicit premises.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the M01 pairwise price calculation and its conditions of applicability."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides trade occurrence and price bounds; the case-specific C004 is not extended into a universal trading condition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Applies the pairwise price to the buyer's payment rate and the seller's receipt rate, while retaining the explanation of budget balance."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Adds the nonnegative-utility requirement for consumer participation, without rewriting it as a proven price-utility equality."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x-p","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The pricing chain provides the pairwise price calculation used by the execution chain, while the execution chain retains the trade and price bounds; this is a functional correspondence across chains and does not copy formulas into R006 or add graph edges."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"],"rationale":"Table 1 implements the same pairwise transaction price as the buyer's payment rate and the seller's receipt rate, respectively; the rate obligations connect to the price calculation but are not duplicate independent rules."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g01-ev-09"],"rationale":"The source text links transaction-price bounds to individual rationality, complementing the nonnegative-utility requirement for buyer participation; this is not used to declare the two constraints equivalent or to fabricate a utility definition."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL004-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R011::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The three chains reference the same M01 pairwise pricing function; only its display is consolidated, without conflating it with the identically named node in the uniform auction."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL004-O02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-BP","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-BP","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x-BP"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"When restricted to the same winning buyer and trading pair, all three reference the same submitted bid price; its role as an execution parameter, its variable roles in the other chains, and the respective omissions of units are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL004-O03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-SP","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-SP","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x-SP"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"When restricted to the same winning seller and trading pair, all three reference the same submitted asking price; no candidate price from any particular bidding strategy is directly treated as this trade input."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL004-O04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-k","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-th-k","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-theta-k"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"],"rationale":"Corresponds to the price weight in the same M01 auction configuration, while retaining parameter records from different stages; the case-study sweep values are not constants simultaneously used in all trades."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R007 has no mathematical object for participation utility; R006 provides transaction-price bounds, while the strategy model has a separate utility based on costs and candidate bids. These three cannot silently be treated as the same utility condition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-09","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g01-ev-15","v141-b-g02-E02"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-05"],"required_work":"Clarify the respective definitions and conditions of participation utility, bidding payoff, and transaction-price bounds, and address the as-yet-unapproved individual-rationality proposal; R007 must not be directly replaced."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The output p in the R009 formula has no separate object in this chain, and R011 also does not declare output objects for the payment and receipt rates. Functional connections across chains can identify their uses, but cannot complete the output declarations, transaction-level indices, and monetary calculations in the frozen catalog.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x-p","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C is to confirm the output objects and transaction-level identities; if this is extended to monetary settlement, obtain the relationship between traded electricity quantities and monetary payments and receipts, without substituting rates for totals."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Budget balance is currently retained as a qualitative property of the settlement chain; the existing settlement node cannot automatically represent a complete operator budget constraint. Units for price objects are also omitted inconsistently across chains.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002","v141-c-R011::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-BP","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-BP"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g01-ev-09","v141-b-g01-ev-10"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-03"],"required_work":"Manually determine how to represent the concept of budget balance and verify the price units; mappings of the same quantity do not overwrite the units or local roles in the original records."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence for pricing, payments and receipts, and individual rationality has not passed independent source review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g01-ev-09","v141-b-g01-ev-10","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify Table 1 and the related explanations of properties; the assembly candidate does not constitute scientific certification of individual rationality or budget balance."}]},"rule_refs":["05-double_auction::v141-c-R009","05-double_auction::v141-c-R006","05-double_auction::v141-c-R011","05-double_auction::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2b436bb00a01fea8","COMP-6057789601b08e93","COMP-d3b88931c4051195","KG31-69ba805a251afd65"]});
